kernel-trim defconfig variant (6.1). Built OK: zImage 3109256 B vs 4431848 B (-1322592, -29.8%); image RAM (_end-_text) 6694984 vs 9423728 B.
Not boot-tested. Apply in steps; each group below is independent. Format: symbols | effect | risk.

ADDED
PRINTK_TIME=y | real timestamps in dmesg | none.
NO_HZ_IDLE=y, HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y | tick stops when idle. samsung_pwm_timer.c:234 clockevent has FEAT_ONESHOT (timer 3 event, 4 source, mach set_timer_source). Both timers are 16 bit at 1320 kHz: max sleep ~49 ms, sched_clock wrap timer also ~24 ms, so ~20-40 wakeups/s instead of 100, not zero | medium: untested timekeeping on this board; first thing to bisect if the boot hangs.
LEGACY_PTYS off | frees 256 BSD pty nodes and sysfs/kernfs entries (PERF sec 2); telnetd uses /dev/pts (build-ttsystem-6.1.sh:80 mounts devpts) | low if busybox telnetd finds /dev/ptmx.
IPV6 off | ~250 KB; usb0 is IPv4 static | low.
I2C=y (+ existing I2C_S3C2410, I2C_CHARDEV=m) | I2C core was silently off (lines dropped by Kconfig). INERT until the board registers s3c_device_i2c0 (devs.c:319; mini2440 also calls s3c_i2c0_set_platdata(NULL)) | low.
BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE=y | makes the existing BACKLIGHT_PWM=m selectable (it was dropped). INERT until backlight-board.patch is applied | low.
DEBUG_INFO_NONE=y | no DWARF: smaller vmlinux/faster build, zImage unchanged. Loses addr2line (System.map still there) | low.
INIT_STACK_NONE=y, STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG off (regular stays) | 1-3 % CPU (estimate), small size | hardening loss; lab device only on usb0.
RTC_DRV_S3C=y kept as built-in. Needs board change in mach-homtom-go630.c: add &s3c_device_rtc to homtom_devices[] (line ~191). devs.c:815 defines it for PLAT_S3C24XX: name s3c2410-rtc, mem S3C24XX_PA_RTC, IRQ_RTC, IRQ_TICK; clk "rtc" alias exists (clk-s3c2443.c:162, PCLKCON bit 12). RTCCON reads 0 today so the driver re-enables it; the time stays invalid until set with hwclock -w.

REMOVED (dead without a registered device or with no consumer in the image)
Netfilter/conntrack/IP_VS/XFRM_USER/NET_KEY/IPIP/INET_AH/ESP/IPCOMP/INET6_*/TCP_CONG_*/IP_PNP*: modules or unused code, nothing in the image loads them; PACKET (udhcpd) and INET kept | low.
CFG80211/MAC80211, BT_HIDP, BT_HCIBCM203X/BPA10X/BFUSB/VHCI: no WiFi hardware, USB BT dongles need a host | low. Kept BT core, HCIUART(BCSP,LL), RFCOMM, BNEP as modules.
USB host stack (USB=y and every USB_* except GADGET, S3C_HSUDC, ETH): board has no OHCI/EHCI device, so usbcore, USB_SERIAL(FTDI,PL2303), USB_MON, storage and sound were dead code (~biggest single saving) | low; gadget ECM is independent.
MTD (CFI, NAND_S3C2410, REDBOOT, ROM...): board file registers no NOR/NAND map. /dev/mtd0 exists only on the stock kernel (flash-safety.md) | low; re-add MTD_PHYSMAP plus a platform device if NOR access from 6.1 is ever wanted.
SCSI/ATA/BLK_DEV_SD/SR/SG, DM9000, PARPORT/PRINTER, NBD, ATA_OVER_ETH, EEPROM_AT24: no hardware path; mmcblk needs only BLOCK+MMC | low.
Joystick/mouse/USB input, ATI_REMOTE2 etc., GPIO_ROTARY_ENCODER; kept EVDEV, TOUCHSCREEN menu, INPUT_MISC and UINPUT=m | low.
SERIAL_8250*, SERIAL_NONSTANDARD, HW_RANDOM, I2C_SIMTEC, SPI*, SENSORS_*, MFD_SM501, TPS65010, LEDS_*: no matching device; ttySAC (SERIAL_SAMSUNG) kept | low. SPI drivers return with the audio codec work.
SOUND/SND*: no machine driver yet (workspace/audio-backlight/asoc-sketch.c is a sketch) | low; re-enable with SND_SOC + the machine driver.
SDIO_UART, MMC_TEST, MMC_SPI: dead; MMC, SDHCI_S3C, MMC_S3C kept | low.
ISO9660/JOLIET, UDF, NTFS, JFFS2, CRAMFS, ROMFS, SQUASHFS, NFS client/ROOT_NFS/NFSD, CIFS, AUTOFS4, FUSE, CONFIGFS: no mounts of these in the image; VFAT/MSDOS/EXT2/EXT3/TMPFS/DEVTMPFS kept; NLS limited to 437/850/ISO8859_1/ASCII/UTF8 | low.
PARTITION_ADVANCED, BSD_DISKLABEL, SOLARIS_X86: DOS partitions stay on by default | low.
DEBUG_MUTEXES: lock debugging overhead | none.

NOT CHANGED, on purpose
VT stays: fbt_console (homtom-fbtext.c:220) has no .device, so /dev/console only works through the VT console. MAX_NR_CONSOLES is a fixed 63 in uapi vt.h, not a Kconfig option.
DEBUG_USER and cmdline user_debug=31, CMDLINE, ignore_loglevel: lab debugging aids, left to a cmdline decision.
Panic: no panic=N and PANIC_TIMEOUT stays 0. Recovery after a panic is the s3c2410 WDT (tmr_atboot=1, userland feeder stops), not the in-kernel restart (LESSONS).
HZ=100, SLAB, KERNEL_GZIP: a switch buys <0.2 s or is unmeasured (PERF).

